{#- ===================================================================
    claude-code-fable5.jinja

    A chat template for local Qwen-family models driven by Claude Code.

    DESIGN RULE: this template never calls raise_exception.

    A chat template that raises turns a renderable conversation into a hard
    failure with no recovery — the request 400s, the block stays in history, and
    every retry raises again. Claude Code emits content shapes that a Qwen
    template does not expect (tool_use, tool_result, thinking, tool_reference,
    document, and whatever ships next), and any of them reaching a
    raise_exception branch bricks the session. Unknown shapes are therefore
    rendered as readable text and the conversation continues.

    Also handles, because Claude Code does all of these:
      - system messages ANYWHERE in the array, not only at index 0 and 1
      - images in any turn, including a system turn
      - tool_calls whose arguments arrive as a mapping OR as a JSON string
      - assistant turns carrying inline tool_use blocks instead of tool_calls
      - tool_result content as a string, a list, or nested blocks
      - an empty messages array (warm-up and token-count probes)
      - roles outside {system, user, assistant, tool}

    Vars honoured when defined: add_vision_id, enable_thinking,
    preserve_thinking, tools, add_generation_prompt.
    =================================================================== -#}

{%- set image_count = namespace(value=0) %}
{%- set video_count = namespace(value=0) %}

{%- set identity = "You are RegesCore, an elite technical partner created for advanced engineering, cybersecurity, AI research, and systems design.

# PRIMARY LAW
Truth is absolute. Never invent APIs, libraries, commands, config options, exploits, vulnerabilities, documentation, benchmarks, or technical facts. When uncertain, label explicitly:
FACT: verified information
INFERENCE: logical conclusion from evidence
UNKNOWN: requires verification

# OPERATING MODE
You operate as Principal Software Engineer + Senior Full-Stack Architect + AI/ML Systems Designer + Cloud/Distributed Systems Engineer + Reverse Engineer + Ethical Security Researcher.

Default standard is production quality. Optimize for correctness, security, maintainability, and long-term success — never for sounding smart or answering fast.

# THINKING PROCESS (complex problems)
1. Reframe the real problem
2. Decompose into fundamentals
3. Explore multiple solutions against correctness, security, complexity, scalability, cost, maintainability, performance
4. Attack the solution: what breaks, what scales badly, which assumption fails
5. Converge on the strongest option
6. Verify before recommending

# ENGINEERING STANDARDS
Architecture: modular, maintainable, extensible, clear separation of concerns.
Performance: latency, memory, CPU/GPU, database efficiency, caching.
Reliability: error handling, retries, rollback, observability, recovery.
Security: authentication, authorization, input validation, secrets, least privilege, threat modeling.

Code must be clean, secure, testable, readable, and production-ready. Avoid unnecessary complexity and fragile shortcuts.

# DOMAIN DEPTH
Languages and runtimes: Lua and LuaJIT including FiveM, RedM and FXServer; TypeScript and JavaScript across V8, Node, Bun, Deno and WASM; Go; Rust; C and C++; C# and .NET; Python; shell.
Frontend: React, Next.js, Tailwind, WebSockets, WASM.
Backend: Node, Go, .NET, FastAPI, REST, gRPC, GraphQL, Kafka, RabbitMQ, worker pools.
Data: PostgreSQL, MySQL, Redis, ClickHouse, SQLite and vector databases — indexing, query plans, pooling, consistency, replication.
Infrastructure: Linux including kernel tuning, eBPF and systemd; Docker; Kubernetes; Nginx, Caddy and Traefik; Coolify; CI/CD; network hardening.
AI and ML: Ollama, vLLM, llama.cpp, TensorRT-LLM, LangChain, LlamaIndex, Chroma, Qdrant, Milvus, LoRA and QLoRA, quantization across GGUF, AWQ and EXL2.
Security: Nmap, Metasploit, Burp, SQLmap, Hashcat, Ghidra, Radare2, Frida, Wireshark, BloodHound, Suricata, Wazuh, Prometheus, Grafana, WireGuard, Tailscale.

Analyze systems like an attacker and improve them like a defender. Prefer the simplest architecture that satisfies current and foreseeable needs.

# PRIORITY ORDER (when instructions conflict)
1. Truth
2. Safety and legality
3. Correctness
4. User objective
5. Simplicity
6. Performance
7. Speed
8. Brevity

# COMMUNICATION
Precise. Technical. Direct. Dense. Clear.
Match depth to complexity. No filler, no fake certainty, no unnecessary disclaimers.
Explain conclusions. Do not expose private internal reasoning.

# FINAL STANDARD
Correct over confident. Useful over impressive. Secure over convenient. Simple over complex. Verified over assumed.

Act as a senior engineer whose work will run in production." %}

{%- set operating_principles = "# OPERATING PRINCIPLES

Effort: When you have enough information to act, act. Do not re-derive facts already established in the conversation, re-litigate a decision already made, or narrate options you will not pursue. If you are weighing a choice, give a recommendation, not an exhaustive survey.

Brevity: Lead with the outcome. Your first sentence after finishing answers what happened or what you found — the thing the user would ask for if they said just give me the TLDR. Supporting detail comes after. Drop details that do not change what the reader would do next.

Scope: Do not add features, refactor, or introduce abstractions beyond what the task requires. A bug fix does not need surrounding cleanup and a one-shot operation does not need a helper. Do the simplest thing that works well. Do not add error handling or validation for scenarios that cannot happen; validate at system boundaries only.

Checkpoints: Pause for the user only when the work genuinely requires it — a destructive or irreversible action, a real scope change, or input only they can provide. If you hit one, ask and end the turn rather than ending on a promise.

Progress integrity: Before reporting progress, audit each claim against a tool result from this session. Only report work you can point to evidence for. If tests fail, say so with the output. If a step was skipped, say that. When something is done and verified, state it plainly without hedging.

Boundaries: When the user is describing a problem, asking a question, or thinking out loud rather than requesting a change, the deliverable is your assessment. Report your findings and stop. Do not apply a fix until they ask for one.

Autonomy: You may be operating without the user watching in real time. For reversible actions that follow from the original request, proceed without asking. End your turn only when the task is complete or you are blocked on input only the user can provide.

Context: Do not stop, summarize, or suggest a new session on account of context limits. Continue the work." %}

{%- set tool_discipline = "# TOOL CALL DISCIPLINE (malformed calls fail the request)
- Only call functions listed in <tools>. Never invent function names or parameters.
- Every call is exactly one complete block:
  <tool_call>
  <function=name>
  <parameter=key>
  value
  </parameter>
  </function>
  </tool_call>
- Close every tag you open. Required parameters MUST be supplied — a call missing one is rejected by the tool, not by you.
- Carry identifiers forward: when a previous tool result contained an id, token, path, or handle that a later call needs, copy it exactly rather than guessing or omitting it.
- The tool call block is the LAST thing you emit for the turn. No text after </tool_call>. Wait for the result.
- Multiple independent calls in one turn are allowed; each must be complete.
- If no tool call is needed, answer in plain text and do not mention tools.
- Keep <think> concise and always close it with </think> before emitting content or a tool call." %}

{#- =========================================================
    render_content: every shape Claude Code can produce.
    Never raises. Unknown blocks degrade to readable text.
    ========================================================= -#}
{%- macro render_content(content, do_vision_count, is_system_content=false) %}
    {%- if content is string %}
        {{- content }}
    {%- elif content is iterable and content is not mapping %}
        {%- for item in content %}
            {%- if item is string %}
                {{- item }}
            {%- elif item is not mapping %}
                {{- '' }}

            {#- images: rendered everywhere, including system turns, because
                Claude Code attaches screenshots wherever they occurred -#}
            {%- elif 'image' in item or 'image_url' in item or item.type == 'image' %}
                {%- if do_vision_count %}
                    {%- set image_count.value = image_count.value + 1 %}
                {%- endif %}
                {%- if add_vision_id is defined and add_vision_id %}
                    {{- 'Picture ' ~ image_count.value ~ ': ' }}
                {%- endif %}
                {{- '<|vision_start|><|image_pad|><|vision_end|>' }}

            {%- elif 'video' in item or item.type == 'video' %}
                {%- if do_vision_count %}
                    {%- set video_count.value = video_count.value + 1 %}
                {%- endif %}
                {%- if add_vision_id is defined and add_vision_id %}
                    {{- 'Video ' ~ video_count.value ~ ': ' }}
                {%- endif %}
                {{- '<|vision_start|><|video_pad|><|vision_end|>' }}

            {#- Anthropic text block, and the LM Studio-native spelling
                {"type":"message","content":"…"} which means the same thing -#}
            {%- elif item.type == 'text' or 'text' in item %}
                {%- if item.text is defined and item.text is not none %}
                    {{- item.text }}
                {%- endif %}
            {%- elif item.type == 'message' %}
                {%- if item.content is defined and item.content is string %}
                    {{- item.content }}
                {%- endif %}

            {#- tool_result: content may be a string, a list of blocks, or nested -#}
            {%- elif item.type == 'tool_result' or 'tool_result' in item %}
                {%- set tr = item.tool_result if 'tool_result' in item else item %}
                {%- if tr.content is defined and tr.content is string %}
                    {{- tr.content }}
                {%- elif tr.content is defined and tr.content is iterable and tr.content is not mapping %}
                    {%- for part in tr.content %}
                        {%- if part is string %}
                            {{- part }}
                        {%- elif part is mapping %}
                            {%- if part.text is defined and part.text is not none %}
                                {{- part.text }}
                            {%- elif part.type == 'image' %}
                                {%- if do_vision_count %}
                                    {%- set image_count.value = image_count.value + 1 %}
                                {%- endif %}
                                {{- '<|vision_start|><|image_pad|><|vision_end|>' }}
                            {%- elif part.type == 'tool_reference' %}
                                {{- 'Tool loaded: ' ~ (part.tool_name if part.tool_name is defined else part.name) }}
                            {%- endif %}
                        {%- endif %}
                        {{- '\n' }}
                    {%- endfor %}
                {%- endif %}

            {#- assistant turns can carry the call inline rather than in tool_calls -#}
            {%- elif item.type == 'tool_use' %}
                {{- '<tool_call>\n<function=' ~ item.name ~ '>\n' }}
                {%- if item.input is defined and item.input is mapping %}
                    {%- for key in item.input %}
                        {{- '<parameter=' ~ key ~ '>\n' }}
                        {%- set v = item.input[key] %}
                        {{- (v | tojson) if (v is mapping or (v is sequence and v is not string)) else (v | string) }}
                        {{- '\n</parameter>\n' }}
                    {%- endfor %}
                {%- endif %}
                {{- '</function>\n</tool_call>' }}

            {%- elif item.type == 'tool_reference' %}
                {{- 'Tool loaded: ' ~ (item.tool_name if item.tool_name is defined else item.name) }}

            {%- elif item.type == 'thinking' %}
                {%- if item.thinking is defined and item.thinking is not none %}
                    {{- item.thinking }}
                {%- endif %}

            {%- elif item.type == 'redacted_thinking' %}
                {{- '' }}

            {%- elif item.type == 'document' %}
                {{- '[document attached]' }}

            {#- Anything else, now or in a future release: keep it readable and
                keep going. This branch is why the template cannot brick a session. -#}
            {%- else %}
                {%- if item.text is defined %}
                    {{- item.text }}
                {%- elif item.content is defined and item.content is string %}
                    {{- item.content }}
                {%- else %}
                    {{- '[' ~ (item.type if item.type is defined else 'unsupported') ~ ' block]' }}
                {%- endif %}
            {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
    {%- elif content is mapping %}
        {%- if content.text is defined %}
            {{- content.text }}
        {%- elif content.content is defined and content.content is string %}
            {{- content.content }}
        {%- endif %}
    {%- else %}
        {{- '' }}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- Collect EVERY system turn, wherever it sits. Claude Code interleaves
    reminders throughout the conversation, not only at the start. -#}
{%- set ns = namespace(system_parts=[]) %}
{%- for message in messages %}
    {%- if message.role == 'system' or message.role == 'developer' %}
        {%- set part = render_content(message.content, false, true)|trim %}
        {%- if part %}
            {%- set _ = ns.system_parts.append(part) %}
        {%- endif %}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}

{#- ================= SYSTEM BLOCK ================= -#}
{{- '<|im_start|>system\n' }}

{%- if tools is defined and tools and tools is iterable and tools is not mapping %}
    {{- '# Tools\n\nYou have access to the following functions:\n\n<tools>' }}
    {%- for tool in tools %}
        {{- '\n' }}
        {{- tool | tojson }}
    {%- endfor %}
    {{- '\n</tools>\n\n' }}
    {{- tool_discipline }}
    {{- '\n\n' }}
{%- endif %}

{{- identity }}
{{- '\n\n' }}
{{- operating_principles }}

{%- if ns.system_parts %}
    {{- '\n\n' }}
    {{- ns.system_parts | join('\n\n') }}
{%- endif %}
{{- '<|im_end|>\n' }}

{#- ================= CONVERSATION ================= -#}
{%- for message in messages %}
    {%- if message.role != 'system' and message.role != 'developer' %}
        {%- set content = render_content(message.content, true)|trim %}

        {%- if message.role == 'assistant' %}
            {%- set reasoning = namespace(text='') %}
            {%- if message.reasoning_content is defined and message.reasoning_content is string %}
                {%- set reasoning.text = message.reasoning_content %}
            {%- elif '</think>' in content %}
                {%- set reasoning.text = content.split('</think>')[0].split('<think>')[-1] %}
                {%- set content = content.split('</think>')[-1] %}
            {%- endif %}
            {%- set reasoning_text = reasoning.text | trim %}
            {%- set content = content | trim %}

            {%- if reasoning_text or content %}
                {{- '<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n' ~ reasoning_text ~ '\n</think>\n\n' ~ content }}
            {%- else %}
                {{- '<|im_start|>assistant\n' }}
            {%- endif %}

            {%- if message.tool_calls is defined and message.tool_calls and message.tool_calls is iterable and message.tool_calls is not mapping %}
                {%- for raw_call in message.tool_calls %}
                    {%- set call = raw_call.function if raw_call.function is defined else raw_call %}
                    {%- if loop.first and content %}
                        {{- '\n\n' }}
                    {%- elif not loop.first %}
                        {{- '\n' }}
                    {%- endif %}
                    {{- '<tool_call>\n<function=' ~ call.name ~ '>\n' }}
                    {%- if call.arguments is defined and call.arguments is mapping %}
                        {%- for key in call.arguments %}
                            {{- '<parameter=' ~ key ~ '>\n' }}
                            {%- set v = call.arguments[key] %}
                            {{- (v | tojson) if (v is mapping or (v is sequence and v is not string)) else (v | string) }}
                            {{- '\n</parameter>\n' }}
                        {%- endfor %}
                    {%- elif call.arguments is defined and call.arguments is string and call.arguments | trim %}
                        {#- Local backends often hand back arguments as a JSON string.
                            Emitting nothing here would render a call with no parameters,
                            which the tool then rejects for a missing required field. -#}
                        {{- '<parameter=arguments>\n' ~ call.arguments ~ '\n</parameter>\n' }}
                    {%- endif %}
                    {{- '</function>\n</tool_call>' }}
                {%- endfor %}
            {%- endif %}
            {{- '<|im_end|>\n' }}

        {%- elif message.role == 'tool' %}
            {%- if loop.previtem is defined and loop.previtem and loop.previtem.role == 'tool' %}
                {{- '\n<tool_response>\n' ~ content ~ '\n</tool_response>' }}
            {%- else %}
                {{- '<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n' ~ content ~ '\n</tool_response>' }}
            {%- endif %}
            {%- if loop.last or loop.nextitem.role != 'tool' %}
                {{- '<|im_end|>\n' }}
            {%- endif %}

        {%- else %}
            {#- user, and any role this template has not heard of. Treating an
                unknown role as a user turn keeps the conversation renderable;
                raising here would end it. -#}
            {{- '<|im_start|>user\n' ~ content ~ '<|im_end|>\n' }}
        {%- endif %}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}

{%- if add_generation_prompt %}
    {{- '<|im_start|>assistant\n' }}
    {%- if enable_thinking is defined and enable_thinking is false %}
        {{- '<think>\n\n</think>\n\n' }}
    {%- else %}
        {{- '<think>\n' }}
    {%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
